//==
// # Law runner: witnesses meshed and validated once (complexity sweep, chunk L7)
//
// What the law runner builds once per model witness so that every run over it reads the same
// values: the outcome of meshing it under layer 8's witness options and the three validation
// reports the runs read (the model's own laws, the mesh's, and the cross checks), each computed
// once. Before this, the runner meshed a positive witness four times for its check runs and the
// three outcome laws, and 2E + 4 times more for its metamorphic laws.

// A model witness meshed once under the witness options, with the three validation reports at
// the Oracle level the runner's laws read, and the laws the witness is built to fail.
// Invariant: Meshed.Outcome is Meshed.Model.MeshModel(MeshingOptions.WitnessOptions);
// ModelChecks is the model's ValidateBrep(Oracle); MeshChecks is ValidateModelMesh of
// Meshed.Outcome.Mesh with the model's tolerances, the witness options' quality thresholds and the
// Oracle level; CrossChecks is the model's CrossCheck of that mesh at Oracle with the witness
// options' face criteria. When the witness options validate at Oracle and the model is runnable,
// the three reports are the parts the outcome's report merged, computed once.
type CheckedWitness
{
    Meshed: MeshedWitness;
    ModelChecks: Report;
    MeshChecks: Report;
    CrossChecks: Report;
    ExpectedFailures: Array<String>;
}

// The three hollow-box laws' verdicts on one drawn sample, from one mesh of it.
type HollowBoxVerdicts
{
    VoidMeshVolumeNegative: Boolean;
    OuterMeshVolumePositive: Boolean;
    MeshVolumeIsDifference: Boolean;
}
